From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:02:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 044/207] Merge dsv41/the Bert port (d75c2e0bf) into candidate
 E: P5 depth overhead, P2 index iota, P3a rotation fold

Ports of Bertholomus's dsv41 decode mechanisms (credits in docs/credits.md):
TF_DSV41_DEPTH_OVERHEAD_MS, TF_DSV41_IDX_IOTA, TF_DSV41_ROT_FOLD.
Conflict: serve_knobs_apply.zig applies and logs D's IDX_SPLIT alongside IDX_IOTA and ROT_FOLD
(iota engages only where an index top-k takes every entry, the split only on long prefill segments).

Co-authored-by: bertholomus <311723197+bertholomus@users.noreply.github.com>

Squashed merge of 4 commits:
- deepseek: price a fixed round overhead into draft depth (TF_DSV41_DEPTH_OVERHEAD_MS) (Jay Leaton)
- docs: credit Bertholomus's dsv41 decode mechanisms (Jay Leaton)
- deepseek: skip index scores whose top-k takes every entry (TF_DSV41_IDX_IOTA) (Jay Leaton)
- deepseek: fold wo_b's input rotation into wo_a's epilogue (TF_DSV41_ROT_FOLD=1) (Jay Leaton)
